## The machine is the relay's (port/web/fly.toml), whose packets are a game's:
## this takes a CPU only when the relay leaves one (fly_start.sh runs it at
## the lowest priority too), and little of the allowance the machine's CPUs
## share.

## one scheduler (its work is small), and one for long native calls
+S 1:1
+SDcpu 1:1

## a scheduler with nothing to do sleeps at once: by default it spins for a
## while first, looking for work
+sbwt none
+sbwtdcpu none
+sbwtdio none
